@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### 1. Create a category: Electronics
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Electronics"
}

### 2. List all categories (should show Electronics, isDeleted=false)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/categories

### 3. Create a product: Laptop (categoryId=1, demonstrates createdDate == modifiedDate on Add)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Laptop",
  "price": 1200.00,
  "categoryId": 1
}

### 4. List all products
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products

### 5. Get product by id (should show createdDate == modifiedDate)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1

### 6. Update product (demonstrates modifiedDate advancing, auditing on Modify)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Laptop Pro",
  "price": 1400.00,
  "categoryId": 1
}

### 7. Get product by id again (modifiedDate should be later than createdDate)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1

### 8. Soft-delete category (Electronics - ISoftDelete entity)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/categories/1

### 9. List all categories (Electronics should be gone - query filter hides soft-deleted)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/categories

### 10. List all categories including deleted (Electronics still visible with isDeleted=true)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/categories/all

### 11. Hard-delete product (Product has no ISoftDelete, so it's physically removed)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1

### 12. List all products (Laptop should be fully gone - hard delete)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products
